Report
------

This ascension is not remarkable because of its conducts; 
actually I see them as the easier half of all possible conducts 
(maybe except vegetarian/vegan).  

It is remarkable since I finally, finally managed to ascend a 
*Barbarian*.  Yes!  At last, Baba fills the ranks of ascended 
classes.  Might be a strange thing, but my Barbarians up to now 
always screwed up badly.  

The game itself went rather smoothly; an easy early start was 
made by finding not only Sunsword but even Vorpal Blade early.  
Some tight moments with soldier ants befor Sokoban; Elbereth 
helped.  After the mines, I stumbled over a brown pudding and 
started to farm a little; I stopped, however, at roughly the 
natural extinction number.  Nonetheless, this farming, which 
costed me just 4.5k turns and two hours playtime, resulted in 

- identify 
- cancellation 
- blessed scroll of remove curse 
- and subsequently, holy water 
- plus quite some healing/energy potions 
(besides 3 1/2 tons of useless junk)

thus boosting my HP to some 180ish.  Additionally, I got some 
enchant scrolls which brought Vorpal Blade to +7 and the saber 
to +6 (lost one + later on a disenchanter), and my AC down to 
-12.  Soko had brought reflection (phew!), and I found a bag 
of holding there, too (nice), so my only worry was MR then.  
After some traveling, I finally found two scrolls of genocide; 
one revealed 6(!) grey dragon scales, while the other gave tele 
control.  Sadly, I didn't have any enchant scrolls left, and, 
during the whole game, did not find a single magic marker, so 
I went off to Medusa with AC -9, wearing the scales.  Medusa 
was the titan level, but a kind soldier provided me a death wand 
a level before, so no worries.  After cleaning up at the castle, 
I decided to have some further blessing-dipping-quaffing round 
to get ~280HP, and some dipping-enchanting, which brought me 
down again to AC -15.  Sadly, I missed a decent MC armor (forgot 
to skin the priest in mine town), so I just went with an elven 
cloak.  Gehennom was as dull as ever; I just noted that you get 
a little more healing potions with Vorpal Blade because of the 
instakill.  Finding the vibrating square without digging up the 
whole place, but having it dug up partially by umber hulks is no 
fun, but by the nice level-port trick I could avoid some 
meaningless, dull slaughter which attracts Rodney.  Speaking of, 
he appeared quite often (never had an aura, just felt nervous 
one time), but always conveniently timed it just some turns after 
a cockatrice corpse went into the BoH, the sweet guy ;-).  
Controlled teleport makes the way up much less painful.  I found 
two pet purple worms on Lvl 46, but lost them on the planes (first 
didn't come with me to earth, second assumedly died on air).  Fun 
comrades, they are.  Buurp!  Despite my HP of ~520, I was a bit 
worried about my AC of -17, but conflict really turns the odds.  
While most people were busy killing each other on astral, my char 
raced through middle, then left, then right altar (Death cut my HP 
badly, though), sometimes dealing out death rays (used a total of 
five, had 10-20 more with recharging), and decided to pull no more 
stunts here but just #offer the damn amulet and be done.  

Whew.  Not so hard to ascend a Barbarian after all ;-).  

Atheist has some edges, but polyless was the really interesting 
difference to me.  Quite some fun.  Next month I'll start to tackle 
illiterate; I have no idea on how to play this (don't tell me, it's 
always fun to find out).  

